## Deriving $t_{\left( r \right)}$

Before we jump into the Kaluza-Klein model, let's investigate the radial time dilation scalar according to General Relativity as this establishes an important relationship for our geometry.

Let's consider that according to Einstein's theory of General Relativity, time dilation at some distance $r$ is described by the following:

$$
t_{\text{GR}} = \sqrt{1 - 2 \frac{GM}{Rc^{2}}}
$$


As the coordinate transformations being proposed interpret time as nothing but the dilation of space, we should define a function that is the inverse of $t_{\text{GR}}$ as

$$
t_{\left( R \right)} = \frac{1}{t_{\text{GR}}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1 - 2 \frac{GM}{Rc^{2}}}}
$$

This then gives a relationship where for $v_{\left( \gamma \right)}$, where


$$
v_{\left( \gamma \right)} = c \sqrt{1 - \frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}}
$$

which can be easily derived by solving Einstein's equation for $\gamma$ for $v$.

We then find

$$
v_{\left( t_{\left( R \right)} \right)} = \sqrt{2 \frac{GM}{R}} = \text{Escape Velocity}
$$


Let's then consider the fact that the escape velocity is given by

$$
\begin{aligned}
E_{\text{Kinetic}} & = \int g ~ dR \\
\frac{1}{2}mv^{2} & = \int G \frac{M}{R^{2}} ~ dR \\
v & = \sqrt{2GM \int \frac{1}{R^{2}}}
\end{aligned}
$$


And Kinetic energy in turn is given by

$$
E_{\text{Kinetic}} = \int p ~ dx = \int m \dot{x} ~ dx
$$


For this reason, we should not consider escape velocity when considering spatial dilation, but rather gravitational acceleration. It is only when this quantity is integrated radially that we find the escape velocity.

## Defining the $\mathbf{KK}$ Metric


Let's start with the electromagnetic field tensor.

$$
F^{\mu \nu} = \left[\begin{matrix}0 & - E_{x} & - E_{y} & - E_{z}\\E_{x} & 0 & B_{z} & - B_{y}\\E_{y} & - B_{z} & 0 & B_{x}\\E_{z} & B_{y} & B_{x} & 0\end{matrix}\right] \qquad  F_{\mu \nu} = \left[\begin{matrix}0 & E_{x} & E_{y} & E_{z}\\- E_{x} & 0 & B_{z} & - B_{y}\\- E_{y} & - B_{z} & 0 & B_{x}\\- E_{z} & B_{y} & B_{x} & 0\end{matrix}\right]
$$

Then 

$$
F_{\mu \nu} = \partial_\mu A_{\nu} - \partial_\nu A_{\mu}
$$

Or

$$
F_{\mu \nu} = \left[\begin{matrix}0 & - \frac{\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{x}} \phi{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}}{c} & - \frac{\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{y}} \phi{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}}{c} & - \frac{\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{z}} \phi{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}}{c}\\\frac{\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{x}} \phi{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}}{c} & 0 & - \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{y}} A_{x}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} + \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{x}} A_{y}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} & - \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{z}} A_{x}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} + \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{x}} A_{z}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}\\\frac{\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{y}} \phi{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}}{c} & \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{y}} A_{x}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} - \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{x}} A_{y}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} & 0 & - \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{z}} A_{y}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} + \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{y}} A_{z}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}\\\frac{\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{z}} \phi{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)}}{c} & \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{z}} A_{x}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} - \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{x}} A_{z}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} & \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{z}} A_{y}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} - \frac{\partial}{\partial S_{y}} A_{z}{\left(S_{x},S_{y},S_{z} \right)} & 0\end{matrix}\right]
$$

This gives the following metric when completely expanded, where $\kappa$ acts as a coupling parameter.

$$
g_{AB} = \left[\begin{matrix}\kappa^{2} \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right)^{2} + 1 & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \kappa \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right)\\\kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \bar{v} + \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right)^{2} & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right)\\\kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right)^{2} & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right)\\\kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa^{2} \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right)^{2} & \kappa \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right)\\\kappa \left(- \frac{E_{x} x}{2} - \frac{E_{y} y}{2} - \frac{E_{z} z}{2}\right) & \kappa \left(\frac{B_{y} z}{2} - \frac{B_{z} y}{2} + \frac{E_{x} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa \left(\frac{B_{x} z}{2} + \frac{B_{z} x}{2} + \frac{E_{y} c t}{2}\right) & \kappa \left(\frac{B_{x} y}{2} - \frac{B_{y} x}{2} + \frac{E_{z} c t}{2}\right) & 1\end{matrix}\right]
$$
